# "The chosen color" is no color word in Sunken Citadel's text (CR 612.2): the color is a choice made as it entered and
# kept on the permanent (CR 607.2d), so Trait Doctoring changing "blue" to "red" on it changes nothing it does. It still
# adds blue, and red is not among the colors it may add.

[Bot1 Deck]
Sunken Citadel
Island
Trait Doctoring
Island x4
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Sunken Citadel.Play
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Sunken Citadel)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Colors(Red)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Trait Doctoring
! Bot1.Battlefield.Sunken Citadel.Activate(Ability: one mana; Color: Red)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Sunken Citadel.Activate(Ability: two mana; Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sunken Citadel.Activate(Ability: one mana; Color: Blue)

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Mana = {U}
Bot1.Battlefield.Sunken Citadel.ChosenColor = Blue
